es, Cervantes, Lope de Vega, Calder\u00f3n, and Sor Juana In\u00e9s de la Cruz, among others.", "catalogBreadth": "(HB)", "catalogDistr": "(LA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "Satisfies Option 1.", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite:\u00a0SPAN 2070\u00a0or SPAN 2090, or CASE Q+.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2741, "crseId": 364573, "crseOfferNbr": 4, "subject": "LATA", "catalogNbr": "3031", "titleShort": "Race & Revolution in Americas", "titleLong": "Race and Revolution in the Americas: 1776-1900", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 16772, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "11:40AM", "timeEnd": "12:55PM", "startDt": "08/29/2019", "endDt": "12/10/2019", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "mw26", "firstName": "Margaret", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Washington"}], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "Rockefeller Hall 122", "bldgDescr": "Rockefeller Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "RCK122", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "08/29/2019", "endDt": "12/10/2019", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "AMST", "catalogNbr": "3032", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "ASRC", "catalogNbr": "3031", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "HIST", "catalogNbr": "3031", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "08/29/2019", "sessionEndDt": "12/10/2019", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "This course will examine the \"age of democratic revolutions\" in the Americas from the perspective of the Black Atlantic. During this momentous era, when European monarchies were successfully challenged and constitutional governments created, Blacks fomented their own American revolutions both in the outside of evolving \"New World democracies.\" This course examines the black trajectory in British North America, Latin America, the French (especially Haiti,) the British and the Spanish Caribbean. The course begins with black participation in the U.S. independence War (1776-1781) and concludes with black (non-U.S.) participation in the independence wars against Spain. The course will also briefly address post-emancipation race relations in these American countries.\u00a0", "catalogBreadth": "(GHB)", "catalogDistr": "(HA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2741, "crseId": 353084, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "LATA", "catalogNbr": "3613", "titleShort": "Steel Band", "titleLong": "Cornell Steel Band", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [